IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc28-part24-s752`

-- ccc28-part24a-dangerous-offender.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), sections 752.01 to 753.02 (PART XXIV, Dangerous Offenders and Long-term Offenders):
-- the prosecutor's duty to advise the court, remand for assessment, the finding that an offender is a dangerous offender, the sentence, a
-- later conviction, and the use of a victim's evidence. Layer 1 of part ccc28.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the
-- official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- READING A RESULT. Each decision function answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE: the text's answer is yes on the facts given. JUST FALSE: the text says
-- no in its own words (a condition introduced with "if", "unless", "where", "on", a period it fixes, a flat negative); the branch carries a comment
-- `FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words)` and the quoted words. NOTHING: not covered; the branch carries `NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. The courts' own judgments (satisfied, of the opinion, reasonable grounds, appropriate) are inputs the
-- person states, as "the court is satisfied that ...": the text hands the judgment to the court and the encoding does not guess it.
-- Periods are in days (a count of days between two events), or dates; the core's `Length of time` is used for terms of imprisonment.

§ `Part XXIV, section 752.01: the prosecutor's duty to advise the court`

-- A previous conviction, as ss 752.01 and 753(1.1) need it: the offence (stated as in section 752), the term of imprisonment the offender was
-- sentenced to for it, whether it was committed against the offender's intimate partner, a member of their family or a member of their intimate
-- partner's family, and whether it was a serious personal injury offence (the answer of s 752, taken as an input).
DECLARE `s 752.01 previous conviction` HAS
    `s 752.01 the offence of the previous conviction` IS A `s 752 offence`
    `s 752.01 the term of imprisonment imposed for it` IS A `Length of time`
    `s 752.01 it was committed against the offender's intimate partner, a member of their family or a member of their intimate partner's family` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 752.01 it was a serious personal injury offence, by s 752` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- helper: a previous conviction of a designated offence for which the offender was sentenced to at least two years of imprisonment.
GIVEN previous IS A `s 752.01 previous conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752.01 the previous conviction is of a designated offence with at least two years of imprisonment` MEANS
    `s 752 both hold`
        (`s 752 the offence is a designated offence` (previous's `s 752.01 the offence of the previous conviction`))
        (JUST (`s 752 the length of time is at least` (previous's `s 752.01 the term of imprisonment imposed for it`) `two years`))

-- helper: a previous conviction of an offence committed against such a person that was a designated offence or a serious personal injury offence.
GIVEN previous IS A `s 752.01 previous conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752.01 the previous conviction is of an offence committed against such a person that was a designated offence or a serious personal injury offence` MEANS
    `s 752 both hold`
        (JUST (previous's `s 752.01 it was committed against the offender's intimate partner, a member of their family or a member of their intimate partner's family`))
        (`s 752 either holds`
            (`s 752 the offence is a designated offence` (previous's `s 752.01 the offence of the previous conviction`))
            (previous's `s 752.01 it was a serious personal injury offence, by s 752`))

-- Paragraphs (a) and (b), and the opinion the prosecutor must hold. "if the prosecutor is of the opinion that an offence for which an offender is
-- found guilty is a serious personal injury offence and that (a) ...; or (b) ...": the opinion is the prosecutor's, so it is an input.
-- src:16391 | 752.01 The prosecutor shall advise the court, as soon as feasible after the finding of guilt and in any event before sentence is imposed, whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1), if the prosecutor is of the opinion that an offence for which an offender is found guilty is a serious personal injury offence and that
-- src:16392 | (a) the offence is a designated offence and the offender was convicted previously at least twice of a designated offence and was sentenced to at least two years of imprisonment for each of those previous convictions; or
-- src:16393 | (b) the offender committed the offence against their intimate partner, a member of their family or a member of their intimate partner’s family, and the offender was convicted previously at least twice of an offence that was committed against any such person and that was a designated offence or serious personal injury offence.
@ref s 752.01 (src:16391-16393)
GIVEN `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the offence is a serious personal injury offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `s 752 offence`
      `the offence was committed against the offender's intimate partner, a member of their family or a member of their intimate partner's family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `previous convictions` IS A LIST OF `s 752.01 previous conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752.01 the prosecutor shall advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prosecutor is of the opinion that the offence is a serious personal injury offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the prosecutor is of the opinion that an offence for which an offender is found guilty is a serious personal injury offence and that"
    ELSE `s 752 either holds` `paragraph (a) holds` `paragraph (b) holds`
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) holds` MEANS
            `s 752 both hold`
                (`s 752 the offence is a designated offence` offence)
                (`s 752 at least two of the answers hold` (map `s 752.01 the previous conviction is of a designated offence with at least two years of imprisonment` `previous convictions`))
        `paragraph (b) holds` MEANS
            `s 752 both hold`
                (JUST `the offence was committed against the offender's intimate partner, a member of their family or a member of their intimate partner's family`)
                (`s 752 at least two of the answers hold` (map `s 752.01 the previous conviction is of an offence committed against such a person that was a designated offence or a serious personal injury offence` `previous convictions`))

-- The duty as a regulative rule. "as soon as feasible after the finding of guilt and in any event before sentence is imposed": the clock starts at the
-- finding of guilt (day 0) and the outer limit is the day sentence is imposed; "as soon as feasible" is open-textured and is not computed (fork F1).
DECLARE `s 752.01 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 752.01 advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)`

@ref s 752.01 (src:16391-16393)
GIVEN `the number of days from the finding of guilt to the imposition of sentence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 752.01 action`
`s 752.01 the prosecutor's duty to advise the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    MUST `s 752.01 advise the court whether the prosecutor intends to make an application under subsection 752.1(1)`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the finding of guilt to the imposition of sentence`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the prosecutor` BECAUSE "the prosecutor did not advise the court before sentence was imposed"

-- The same duty's time limit as a decision function: the advice is in time if it is given on or before the day sentence is imposed.
@ref s 752.01 (src:16391-16393)
GIVEN `the number of days from the finding of guilt to the day the prosecutor advised the court` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days from the finding of guilt to the imposition of sentence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752.01 the prosecutor advised the court before sentence was imposed` MEANS
    IF `the number of days from the finding of guilt to the day the prosecutor advised the court` AT MOST `the number of days from the finding of guilt to the imposition of sentence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any event before sentence is imposed"

§ `Part XXIV, section 752.1: remand for assessment`

-- (1) "On application by the prosecutor, if the court is of the opinion that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offender who is convicted of
-- a serious personal injury offence or an offence referred to in paragraph 753.1(2)(a) might be found to be a dangerous offender under section 753 or a
-- long-term offender under section 753.1, the court shall, by order in writing, before sentence is imposed, remand the offender, ...".
-- The answer of s 753.1(2)(a) (which offences it names) is taken as an input, named for that section; it is computed in `ccc28-part24b-long-term`.
-- src:16394 | Application for remand for assessment
-- src:16395 | 752.1 (1) On application by the prosecutor, if the court is of the opinion that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offender who is convicted of a serious personal injury offence or an offence referred to in paragraph 753.1(2)(a) might be found to be a dangerous offender under section 753 or a long-term offender under section 753.1, the court shall, by order in writing, before sentence is imposed, remand the offender, for a period not exceeding 60 days, to the custody of a person designated by the court who can perform an assessment or have an assessment performed by experts for use as evidence in an application under section 753 or 753.1.
@ref s 752.1(1) (src:16394-16395)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is of the opinion that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the offender might be found to be a dangerous offender under section 753 or a long-term offender under section 753.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is convicted of a serious personal injury offence, by s 752` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offender is convicted of an offence referred to in paragraph 753.1(2)(a), by s 753.1(2)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752.1(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prosecutor has applied`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by the prosecutor"
    ELSE IF NOT `the court is of the opinion that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the offender might be found to be a dangerous offender under section 753 or a long-term offender under section 753.1`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court is of the opinion that there are reasonable grounds to believe"
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 752 either holds` `the offender is convicted of a serious personal injury offence, by s 752` `the offender is convicted of an offence referred to in paragraph 753.1(2)(a), by s 753.1(2)(a)`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offender who is convicted of a serious personal injury offence or an offence referred to in paragraph 753.1(2)(a)"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 752 or of s 753.1(2)(a) is itself not covered

-- "for a period not exceeding 60 days".
@ref s 752.1(1) (src:16394-16395)
GIVEN `the number of days of the remand` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752.1(1) the remand is for a period not exceeding 60 days` MEANS
    IF `the number of days of the remand` AT MOST 60
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period not exceeding 60 days"

-- The duty as a regulative rule: the court remands the offender, by order in writing, before sentence is imposed. The 60-day limit on the remand
-- is the decision function above; the rule below does not carry the length of the remand.
DECLARE `s 752.1(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 752.1(1) remand the offender by order in writing to the custody of a person designated by the court`

@ref s 752.1(1) (src:16394-16395)
GIVEN `the number of days from the application to the imposition of sentence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 752.1(1) action`
`s 752.1(1) the court's duty to remand the offender` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 752.1(1) remand the offender by order in writing to the custody of a person designated by the court`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the application to the imposition of sentence`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not remand the offender before sentence was imposed"

-- (2) "The person to whom the offender is remanded shall file a report of the assessment with the court not later than 30 days after the end of the
-- assessment period and make copies of it available to the prosecutor and counsel for the offender." The person is not among the core's `Party`
-- constructors (NEEDS-CORE.md): a party type of this section is declared here.
DECLARE `s 752.1(2) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded`

DECLARE `s 752.1(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 752.1(2) file a report of the assessment with the court`
    `s 752.1(2) make copies of the report available to the prosecutor and counsel for the offender`

-- src:16396 | Report
-- src:16397 | (2) The person to whom the offender is remanded shall file a report of the assessment with the court not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period and make copies of it available to the prosecutor and counsel for the offender.
@ref s 752.1(2) (src:16396-16397)
GIVEN `the number of days by which the court extended the period under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 752.1(2) party` `s 752.1(2) action`
`s 752.1(2) the duty of the person to whom the offender is remanded` MEANS
    PARTY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded`
    MUST `s 752.1(2) file a report of the assessment with the court`
    WITHIN 30 PLUS `the number of days by which the court extended the period under subsection (3)`
    HENCE (PARTY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded`
           MUST `s 752.1(2) make copies of the report available to the prosecutor and counsel for the offender`
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST BREACH BY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded` BECAUSE "copies of the report were not made available to the prosecutor and counsel for the offender")
    LEST BREACH BY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded` BECAUSE "the report was not filed within 30 days after the end of the assessment period"

-- The same limit as a decision function, over a day count (day 0 is the end of the assessment period) and over dates.
@ref s 752.1(2) (src:16396-16397)
GIVEN `the number of days from the end of the assessment period to the filing of the report` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days by which the court extended the period under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752.1(2) the report is filed not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period` MEANS
    IF `the number of days from the end of the assessment period to the filing of the report` AT MOST (30 PLUS `the number of days by which the court extended the period under subsection (3)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period"

@ref s 752.1(2) (src:16396-16397)
GIVEN `the end of the assessment period` IS A DATE
      `the number of days by which the court extended the period under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 752.1(2) the last day on which the report is filed in time` MEANS
    Date (Day `the end of the assessment period` PLUS 30 PLUS `the number of days by which the court extended the period under subsection (3)`)

-- (3) "On application by the prosecutor, the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed by a maximum of 30 days if the court is
-- satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to do so." A power ("may"). Two gates: "On application by the prosecutor" (an "on" gate: JUST FALSE, listed
-- in NOTES.md group (i)); "if the court is satisfied ..." (an "if" gate on a power: NOTHING, fork F3).
-- src:16398 | Extension of time
-- src:16399 | (3) On application by the prosecutor, the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed by a maximum of 30 days if the court is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to do so.
@ref s 752.1(3) (src:16398-16399)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to extend the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752.1(3) the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prosecutor has applied`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by the prosecutor"
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to extend the period`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to do so": a grant limited by an "if" gate; the text does not say the court may not extend otherwise

@ref s 752.1(3) (src:16398-16399)
GIVEN `the number of days of the extension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 752.1(3) the extension is by a maximum of 30 days` MEANS
    IF `the number of days of the extension` AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by a maximum of 30 days"

§ `Part XXIV, section 753: the finding that an offender is a dangerous offender`

-- (1) "On application made under this Part after an assessment report is filed under subsection 752.1(2), the court shall find the offender to be a
-- dangerous offender if it is satisfied (a) that the offence ... is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (a) of the definition ... and
-- the offender constitutes a threat ... on the basis of evidence establishing (i) ..., (ii) ... or (iii) ...; or (b) that the offence ... is a serious
-- personal injury offence described in paragraph (b) ... and the offender, by his or her conduct in any sexual matter ..., has shown a failure to
-- control his or her sexual impulses and a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil to other persons through failure in the future ...".
-- The court's satisfaction is stated as the facts the court is satisfied of; which paragraph of "serious personal injury offence" the offence falls in is
-- taken from `s 752 serious personal injury offence (a)` and `(b)` (inputs here, named for that section).
-- src:16400 | Application for finding that an offender is a dangerous offender
-- src:16401 | 753 (1) On application made under this Part after an assessment report is filed under subsection 752.1(2), the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender if it is satisfied
-- src:16402 | (a) that the offence for which the offender has been convicted is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (a) of the definition of that expression in section 752 and the offender constitutes a threat to the life, safety or physical or mental well-being of other persons on the basis of evidence establishing
-- src:16403 | (i) a pattern of repetitive behaviour by the offender, of which the offence for which he or she has been convicted forms a part, showing a failure to restrain his or her behaviour and a likelihood of causing death or injury to other persons, or inflicting severe psychological damage on other persons, through failure in the future to restrain his or her behaviour,
-- src:16404 | (ii) a pattern of persistent aggressive behaviour by the offender, of which the offence for which he or she has been convicted forms a part, showing a substantial degree of indifference on the part of the offender respecting the reasonably foreseeable consequences to other persons of his or her behaviour, or
-- src:16405 | (iii) any behaviour by the offender, associated with the offence for which he or she has been convicted, that is of such a brutal nature as to compel the conclusion that the offender’s behaviour in the future is unlikely to be inhibited by normal standards of behavioural restraint; or
-- src:16406 | (b) that the offence for which the offender has been convicted is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (b) of the definition of that expression in section 752 and the offender, by his or her conduct in any sexual matter including that involved in the commission of the offence for which he or she has been convicted, has shown a failure to control his or her sexual impulses and a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil to other persons through failure in the future to control his or her sexual impulses.
@ref s 753(1) (src:16400-16406)
GIVEN `an application was made under this Part after an assessment report was filed under subsection 752.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (a) of the definition, by s 752` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (b) of the definition, by s 752` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the offender constitutes a threat to the life, safety or physical or mental well-being of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes a pattern of repetitive behaviour (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes a pattern of persistent aggressive behaviour (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes behaviour of such a brutal nature (iii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the offender has shown a failure to control sexual impulses and a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(1) the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application was made under this Part after an assessment report was filed under subsection 752.1(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application made under this Part after an assessment report is filed under subsection 752.1(2)"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 752 either holds` (`s 752 both hold` `the offence is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (a) of the definition, by s 752` (JUST `paragraph (a) holds`)) (`s 752 both hold` `the offence is a serious personal injury offence described in paragraph (b) of the definition, by s 752` (JUST `paragraph (b) holds`))
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court shall find the offender to be a dangerous offender if it is satisfied"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 752 for paragraph (a) or (b) of "serious personal injury offence" is itself not covered
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) holds` MEANS
                `the court is satisfied that the offender constitutes a threat to the life, safety or physical or mental well-being of other persons`
            AND (    `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes a pattern of repetitive behaviour (i)`
                  OR `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes a pattern of persistent aggressive behaviour (ii)`
                  OR `the court is satisfied that the evidence establishes behaviour of such a brutal nature (iii)`)
        `paragraph (b) holds` MEANS `the court is satisfied that the offender has shown a failure to control sexual impulses and a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil (b)`

-- (1.1) The presumption: "If the court is satisfied that the offence for which the offender is convicted is a primary designated offence for which it
-- would be appropriate to impose a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more and that the offender was convicted previously at least twice of a
-- primary designated offence and was sentenced to at least two years of imprisonment for each of those convictions, the conditions in paragraph (1)(a) or
-- (b), as the case may be, are presumed to have been met unless the contrary is proved on a balance of probabilities."
-- "each of those convictions" is read as the at least two previous convictions counted (fork F2): the offender has at least two previous convictions
-- of a primary designated offence, each with a sentence of at least two years.
-- src:16407 | Presumption
-- src:16408 | (1.1) If the court is satisfied that the offence for which the offender is convicted is a primary designated offence for which it would be appropriate to impose a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more and that the offender was convicted previously at least twice of a primary designated offence and was sentenced to at least two years of imprisonment for each of those convictions, the conditions in paragraph (1)(a) or (b), as the case may be, are presumed to have been met unless the contrary is proved on a balance of probabilities.
@ref s 753(1.1) (src:16407-16408)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 752 offence`
      `the court is satisfied that it would be appropriate to impose a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `previous convictions` IS A LIST OF `s 752.01 previous conviction`
      `the contrary is proved on a balance of probabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(1.1) the conditions in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) are presumed to have been met` MEANS
    IF `the contrary is proved on a balance of probabilities`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the contrary is proved on a balance of probabilities"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 752 both hold`
                      (`s 752 both hold`
                          (`s 752 the offence is a primary designated offence` offence)
                          (JUST `the court is satisfied that it would be appropriate to impose a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more for the offence`))
                      (`s 752 at least two of the answers hold` (map `the previous conviction is of a primary designated offence with at least two years of imprisonment` `previous convictions`))
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court is satisfied that the offence for which the offender is convicted is a primary designated offence for which it would be appropriate to impose a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more and that the offender was convicted previously at least twice of a primary designated offence and was sentenced to at least two years of imprisonment for each of those convictions"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer of s 752 for "primary designated offence" is itself not covered
    WHERE
        `the previous conviction is of a primary designated offence with at least two years of imprisonment` MEANS
            GIVEN previous YIELD
                `s 752 both hold`
                    (`s 752 the offence is a primary designated offence` (previous's `s 752.01 the offence of the previous conviction`))
                    (JUST (`s 752 the length of time is at least` (previous's `s 752.01 the term of imprisonment imposed for it`) `two years`))

-- (2) "An application under subsection (1) must be made before sentence is imposed on the offender unless (a) before the imposition of sentence, the
-- prosecutor gives notice to the offender of a possible intention to make an application under section 752.1 and an application under subsection (1) not
-- later than six months after that imposition; and (b) at the time of the application under subsection (1) that is not later than six months after the
-- imposition of sentence, it is shown that relevant evidence that was not reasonably available to the prosecutor at the time of the imposition of sentence
-- became available in the interim."
-- "six months after" is the date six months later, with the day clamped to the last day of a shorter month (`add months` of daydate; fork F4).
-- src:16409 | Time for making application
-- src:16410 | (2) An application under subsection (1) must be made before sentence is imposed on the offender unless
-- src:16411 | (a) before the imposition of sentence, the prosecutor gives notice to the offender of a possible intention to make an application under section 752.1 and an application under subsection (1) not later than six months after that imposition; and
-- src:16412 | (b) at the time of the application under subsection (1) that is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence, it is shown that relevant evidence that was not reasonably available to the prosecutor at the time of the imposition of sentence became available in the interim.
@ref s 753(2) (src:16409-16412)
GIVEN `the date sentence was imposed` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 753(2) the application is made not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` MEANS
    Day `the date of the application under subsection (1)` AT MOST Day (`add months` `the date sentence was imposed` 6)

@ref s 753(2) (src:16409-16412)
GIVEN `before the imposition of sentence the prosecutor gave the offender notice of a possible intention to make an application under section 752.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date sentence was imposed` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(2)(a) the notice was given and the application is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` MEANS
    IF NOT `before the imposition of sentence the prosecutor gave the offender notice of a possible intention to make an application under section 752.1`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the imposition of sentence, the prosecutor gives notice to the offender of a possible intention to make an application under section 752.1"
    ELSE IF `s 753(2) the application is made not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` `the date sentence was imposed` `the date of the application under subsection (1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an application under subsection (1) not later than six months after that imposition"

@ref s 753(2) (src:16409-16412)
GIVEN `it is shown that relevant evidence that was not reasonably available to the prosecutor at the time of the imposition of sentence became available in the interim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date sentence was imposed` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application under subsection (1)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(2)(b) relevant evidence became available in the interim and the application is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 753(2) the application is made not later than six months after the imposition of sentence` `the date sentence was imposed` `the date of the application under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the time of the application under subsection (1) that is not later than six months after the imposition of sentence"
    ELSE IF `it is shown that relevant evidence that was not reasonably available to the prosecutor at the time of the imposition of sentence became available in the interim`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is shown that relevant evidence that was not reasonably available to the prosecutor at the time of the imposition of sentence became available in the interim"

-- Paragraphs (a) and (b) both apply: the answer of the two functions above combined; the cases the later subsections refer to as "a case to which paragraphs
-- (2)(a) and (b) apply".
@ref s 753(2) (src:16409-16412)
GIVEN `paragraph (2)(a) applies, by s 753(2)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2)(b) applies, by s 753(2)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(2)(a) and (b) apply` MEANS `s 752 both hold` `paragraph (2)(a) applies, by s 753(2)(a)` `paragraph (2)(b) applies, by s 753(2)(b)`

-- "must be made before sentence is imposed on the offender unless (a) and (b)".
@ref s 753(2) (src:16409-16412)
GIVEN `the application under subsection (1) is made before sentence is imposed on the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply, by s 753(2)(a) and (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(2) the application under subsection (1) is made in time` MEANS
    IF `the application under subsection (1) is made before sentence is imposed on the offender`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply, by s 753(2)(a) and (b)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made before sentence is imposed on the offender unless"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) is itself not covered

-- (3) "Notwithstanding subsection 752.1(1), an application under that subsection may be made after the imposition of sentence or after an offender begins
-- to serve the sentence in a case to which paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply." A power ("may"), with a gate of the kind "in a case to which ...": JUST FALSE
-- when the case is not one to which (2)(a) and (b) apply, listed in NOTES.md group (i) (the other reading: NOTHING).
-- src:16413 | Application for remand for assessment after imposition of sentence
-- src:16414 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection 752.1(1), an application under that subsection may be made after the imposition of sentence or after an offender begins to serve the sentence in a case to which paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply.
@ref s 753(3) (src:16413-16414)
GIVEN `paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply, by s 753(2)(a) and (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(3) an application under subsection 752.1(1) may be made after the imposition of sentence or after the offender begins to serve the sentence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply, by s 753(2)(a) and (b)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case to which paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) is itself not covered

-- (4) "If the court finds an offender to be a dangerous offender, it shall (a) impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate
-- period; (b) impose a sentence for the offence ... -- which must be a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years -- and order that the
-- offender be subject to long-term supervision for a period that does not exceed 10 years; or (c) impose a sentence for the offence ...".
DECLARE `s 753(4) disposition` IS ONE OF
    `s 753(4)(a) a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period`
    `s 753(4)(b) a sentence for the offence with an order for long-term supervision` HAS `s 753(4)(b) the term of imprisonment` IS A `Length of time`
                                                                                         `s 753(4)(b) the period of long-term supervision` IS A `Length of time`
    `s 753(4)(c) a sentence for the offence`
    `s 753(4) a disposition the subsection does not name`

-- src:16415 | Sentence for dangerous offender
-- src:16416 | (4) If the court finds an offender to be a dangerous offender, it shall
-- src:16417 | (a) impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period;
-- src:16418 | (b) impose a sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted — which must be a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years — and order that the offender be subject to long-term supervision for a period that does not exceed 10 years; or
-- src:16419 | (c) impose a sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted.
@ref s 753(4) (src:16415-16419)
GIVEN `the court has found the offender to be a dangerous offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      disposition IS A `s 753(4) disposition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(4) the disposition is within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court has found the offender to be a dangerous offender`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court finds an offender to be a dangerous offender"
    ELSE CONSIDER disposition
         WHEN `s 753(4)(a) a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753(4)(b) a sentence for the offence with an order for long-term supervision` term period THEN
             IF NOT `s 752 the length of time is at least` term `two years`
             THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which must be a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years"
             ELSE IF NOT `s 752 the length of time is at least` `ten years` period
                  THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period that does not exceed 10 years"
                  ELSE JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753(4)(c) a sentence for the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753(4) a disposition the subsection does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraphs (a) to (c) are not closed with "only"

-- (4.1) "The court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period unless it is satisfied by the evidence adduced
-- during the hearing of the application that there is a reasonable expectation that a lesser measure under paragraph (4)(b) or (c) will adequately protect
-- the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious personal injury offence."
-- src:16420 | Sentence of indeterminate detention
-- src:16421 | (4.1) The court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period unless it is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing of the application that there is a reasonable expectation that a lesser measure under paragraph (4)(b) or (c) will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious personal injury offence.
@ref s 753(4.1) (src:16420-16421)
GIVEN `the court has found the offender to be a dangerous offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing that there is a reasonable expectation that a lesser measure under paragraph (4)(b) or (c) will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious personal injury offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(4.1) the court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court has found the offender to be a dangerous offender`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection does not say what the court does when it has not found the offender to be a dangerous offender; subsection (5) does
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing that there is a reasonable expectation that a lesser measure under paragraph (4)(b) or (c) will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious personal injury offence`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing of the application"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4.2) "If the application is made after the offender begins to serve the sentence in a case to which paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply, a sentence imposed
-- under paragraph (4)(a), or a sentence imposed and an order made under paragraph 4(b), replaces the sentence that was imposed for the offence ...".
-- src:16422 | If application made after sentencing
-- src:16423 | (4.2) If the application is made after the offender begins to serve the sentence in a case to which paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply, a sentence imposed under paragraph (4)(a), or a sentence imposed and an order made under paragraph 4(b), replaces the sentence that was imposed for the offence for which the offender was convicted.
@ref s 753(4.2) (src:16422-16423)
GIVEN `the application is made after the offender begins to serve the sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply, by s 753(2)(a) and (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      disposition IS A `s 753(4) disposition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(4.2) the sentence imposed replaces the sentence that was imposed for the offence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application is made after the offender begins to serve the sentence`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the application is made after the offender begins to serve the sentence"
    ELSE CONSIDER `paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply, by s 753(2)(a) and (b)`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case to which paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) apply"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) is itself not covered
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             CONSIDER disposition
             WHEN `s 753(4)(a) a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 753(4)(b) a sentence for the offence with an order for long-term supervision` term period THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 753(4)(c) a sentence for the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names a sentence under paragraph (4)(a) and a sentence and order under paragraph (4)(b), not a sentence under (4)(c)
             WHEN `s 753(4) a disposition the subsection does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not named in the subsection

-- (5) "If the court does not find an offender to be a dangerous offender, (a) the court may treat the application as an application to find the offender to
-- be a long-term offender, section 753.1 applies to the application and the court may either find that the offender is a long-term offender or hold another
-- hearing for that purpose; or (b) the court may impose sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted." Powers ("may") under an "if"
-- gate: NOTHING when the gate fails (fork F3).
DECLARE `s 753(5) course` IS ONE OF
    `s 753(5)(a) treat the application as an application to find the offender to be a long-term offender`
    `s 753(5)(a) find that the offender is a long-term offender`
    `s 753(5)(a) hold another hearing for that purpose`
    `s 753(5)(b) impose sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted`
    `s 753(5) a course the subsection does not name`

-- src:16424 | If offender not found to be dangerous offender
-- src:16425 | (5) If the court does not find an offender to be a dangerous offender,
-- src:16426 | (a) the court may treat the application as an application to find the offender to be a long-term offender, section 753.1 applies to the application and the court may either find that the offender is a long-term offender or hold another hearing for that purpose; or
-- src:16427 | (b) the court may impose sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted.
@ref s 753(5) (src:16424-16427)
GIVEN `the court does not find the offender to be a dangerous offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      course IS A `s 753(5) course`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753(5) the court may take this course` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court does not find the offender to be a dangerous offender`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court does not find an offender to be a dangerous offender": a grant limited by an "if" gate; the text does not say the court may not take the course otherwise
    ELSE CONSIDER course
         WHEN `s 753(5)(a) treat the application as an application to find the offender to be a long-term offender` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753(5)(a) find that the offender is a long-term offender` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753(5)(a) hold another hearing for that purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753(5)(b) impose sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753(5) a course the subsection does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (a) and (b) are not closed with "only"

§ `Part XXIV, section 753.01: remand and a new sentence after a later conviction`

-- (1) "If an offender who is found to be a dangerous offender is later convicted of a serious personal injury offence or an offence under subsection
-- 753.3(1), on application by the prosecutor, the court shall, by order in writing, before sentence is imposed, remand the offender, for a period not
-- exceeding 60 days, ...".
-- src:16429 | Application for remand for assessment — later conviction
-- src:16430 | 753.01 (1) If an offender who is found to be a dangerous offender is later convicted of a serious personal injury offence or an offence under subsection 753.3(1), on application by the prosecutor, the court shall, by order in writing, before sentence is imposed, remand the offender, for a period not exceeding 60 days, to the custody of a person designated by the court who can perform an assessment or have an assessment performed by experts for use as evidence in an application under subsection (4).
@ref s 753.01(1) (src:16429-16430)
GIVEN `the offender was found to be a dangerous offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is later convicted of a serious personal injury offence, by s 752` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offender is later convicted of an offence under subsection 753.3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.01(1) the court shall remand the offender for an assessment` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offender was found to be a dangerous offender`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offender who is found to be a dangerous offender is later convicted of"
    ELSE IF NOT `the prosecutor has applied`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application by the prosecutor"
         ELSE IF `the offender is later convicted of an offence under subsection 753.3(1)`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE CONSIDER `the offender is later convicted of a serious personal injury offence, by s 752`
                   WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                   WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is later convicted of a serious personal injury offence or an offence under subsection 753.3(1)"
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 752 for "serious personal injury offence" is itself not covered

@ref s 753.01(1) (src:16429-16430)
GIVEN `the number of days of the remand` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.01(1) the remand is for a period not exceeding 60 days` MEANS
    IF `the number of days of the remand` AT MOST 60
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period not exceeding 60 days"

-- (2) The report: the same duty as section 752.1(2), on the person to whom the offender is remanded under subsection (1).
DECLARE `s 753.01(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 753.01(2) file a report of the assessment with the court`
    `s 753.01(2) make copies of the report available to the prosecutor and counsel for the offender`

-- src:16431 | Report
-- src:16432 | (2) The person to whom the offender is remanded shall file a report of the assessment with the court not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period and make copies of it available to the prosecutor and counsel for the offender.
@ref s 753.01(2) (src:16431-16432)
GIVEN `the number of days by which the court extended the period under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 752.1(2) party` `s 753.01(2) action`
`s 753.01(2) the duty of the person to whom the offender is remanded` MEANS
    PARTY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded`
    MUST `s 753.01(2) file a report of the assessment with the court`
    WITHIN 30 PLUS `the number of days by which the court extended the period under subsection (3)`
    HENCE (PARTY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded`
           MUST `s 753.01(2) make copies of the report available to the prosecutor and counsel for the offender`
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST BREACH BY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded` BECAUSE "copies of the report were not made available to the prosecutor and counsel for the offender")
    LEST BREACH BY `s 752.1(2) the person to whom the offender is remanded` BECAUSE "the report was not filed within 30 days after the end of the assessment period"

@ref s 753.01(2) (src:16431-16432)
GIVEN `the number of days from the end of the assessment period to the filing of the report` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days by which the court extended the period under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.01(2) the report is filed not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period` MEANS
    IF `the number of days from the end of the assessment period to the filing of the report` AT MOST (30 PLUS `the number of days by which the court extended the period under subsection (3)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than 30 days after the end of the assessment period"

-- (3) "On application by the prosecutor, the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed by a maximum of 30 days if the court is
-- satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to do so." The same two gates as section 752.1(3).
-- src:16433 | Extension of time
-- src:16434 | (3) On application by the prosecutor, the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed by a maximum of 30 days if the court is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to do so.
@ref s 753.01(3) (src:16433-16434)
GIVEN `the prosecutor has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to extend the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.01(3) the court may extend the period within which the report must be filed` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prosecutor has applied`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by the prosecutor"
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to extend the period`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to do so": a grant limited by an "if" gate; the text does not say the court may not extend otherwise

@ref s 753.01(3) (src:16433-16434)
GIVEN `the number of days of the extension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.01(3) the extension is by a maximum of 30 days` MEANS
    IF `the number of days of the extension` AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by a maximum of 30 days"

-- (4) "After the report is filed, the prosecutor may apply for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period, or for an order that
-- the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision in addition to any other sentence that may be imposed for the offence." A power
-- ("may") with a gate of the kind "After ...": JUST FALSE before the report is filed, listed in NOTES.md group (i) (the other reading: NOTHING).
DECLARE `s 753.01(4) application` IS ONE OF
    `s 753.01(4) an application for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period`
    `s 753.01(4) an application for an order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision`
    `s 753.01(4) an application the subsection does not name`

-- src:16435 | Application for new sentence or order
-- src:16436 | (4) After the report is filed, the prosecutor may apply for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period, or for an order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision in addition to any other sentence that may be imposed for the offence.
@ref s 753.01(4) (src:16435-16436)
GIVEN `the report has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      application IS A `s 753.01(4) application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.01(4) the prosecutor may apply for this sentence or order` MEANS
    IF NOT `the report has been filed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After the report is filed"
    ELSE CONSIDER application
         WHEN `s 753.01(4) an application for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753.01(4) an application for an order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753.01(4) an application the subsection does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the two applications are not closed with "only"

-- (5) "If the application is for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period, the court shall impose that sentence unless it is
-- satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing of the application that there is a reasonable expectation that a sentence for the offence ... --
-- with or without a new period of long-term supervision -- will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a
-- serious personal injury offence."
-- src:16437 | Sentence of indeterminate detention
-- src:16438 | (5) If the application is for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period, the court shall impose that sentence unless it is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing of the application that there is a reasonable expectation that a sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted — with or without a new period of long-term supervision — will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious personal injury offence.
@ref s 753.01(5) (src:16437-16438)
GIVEN `the application is for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing that there is a reasonable expectation that a sentence for the offence, with or without a new period of long-term supervision, will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious personal injury offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.01(5) the court shall impose a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application is for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the application is for a sentence of detention in a penitentiary for an indeterminate period"
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing that there is a reasonable expectation that a sentence for the offence, with or without a new period of long-term supervision, will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious personal injury offence`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing of the application"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (6) "If the application is for a new period of long-term supervision, the court shall order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term
-- supervision in addition to a sentence for the offence ... unless it is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing of the application that there
-- is a reasonable expectation that the sentence alone will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious
-- personal injury offence."
-- src:16439 | New long-term supervision
-- src:16440 | (6) If the application is for a new period of long-term supervision, the court shall order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision in addition to a sentence for the offence for which they have been convicted unless it is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing of the application that there is a reasonable expectation that the sentence alone will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious personal injury offence.
@ref s 753.01(6) (src:16439-16440)
GIVEN `the application is for a new period of long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing that there is a reasonable expectation that the sentence alone will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious personal injury offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.01(6) the court shall order that the offender be subject to a new period of long-term supervision` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application is for a new period of long-term supervision`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the application is for a new period of long-term supervision"
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing that there is a reasonable expectation that the sentence alone will adequately protect the public against the commission by the offender of murder or a serious personal injury offence`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is satisfied by the evidence adduced during the hearing of the application"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Part XXIV, section 753.02: a victim's evidence`

-- "Any evidence given during the hearing of an application made under subsection 753(1) by a victim of an offence for which the offender was convicted is
-- deemed also to have been given during any hearing held with respect to the offender under paragraph 753(5)(a) or subsection 753.01(5) or (6)."
DECLARE `s 753.02 hearing` IS ONE OF
    `s 753.02 a hearing under paragraph 753(5)(a)`
    `s 753.02 a hearing under subsection 753.01(5)`
    `s 753.02 a hearing under subsection 753.01(6)`
    `s 753.02 a hearing the section does not name`

-- src:16441 | Victim evidence
-- src:16442 | 753.02 Any evidence given during the hearing of an application made under subsection 753(1) by a victim of an offence for which the offender was convicted is deemed also to have been given during any hearing held with respect to the offender under paragraph 753(5)(a) or subsection 753.01(5) or (6).
@ref s 753.02 (src:16441-16442)
GIVEN `the evidence was given during the hearing of an application made under subsection 753(1) by a victim of an offence for which the offender was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      hearing IS A `s 753.02 hearing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.02 the evidence is deemed also to have been given during the hearing` MEANS
    IF NOT `the evidence was given during the hearing of an application made under subsection 753(1) by a victim of an offence for which the offender was convicted`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any evidence given during the hearing of an application made under subsection 753(1) by a victim": the deeming is limited to that evidence; the section is silent on other evidence
    ELSE CONSIDER hearing
         WHEN `s 753.02 a hearing under paragraph 753(5)(a)` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753.02 a hearing under subsection 753.01(5)` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753.02 a hearing under subsection 753.01(6)` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753.02 a hearing the section does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any hearing held with respect to the offender under paragraph 753(5)(a) or subsection 753.01(5) or (6)": the deeming reaches those hearings only by its words, and the section does not say it reaches no other
